  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reduction of greenhouse gas emissions by enhancing efficiency and transparency in Pakistan&apos;s leather industry</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Climate Change requested UNIDO to contribute technical assistance to reduce environmental footprint of the leather sector. The project would be the 3rd GEF project for UNIDO in Pakistan related to the leather industry (160069 and 150052).  The project supports Pakistan#s transition toward a low-carbon, resource-efficient, and transparent leather sector. Anchored in the Sialkot Tannery Zone (STZ), a GEF/UNIDO-backed industrial cluster with a Common Effluent Treatment Plant, the project will accelerate uptake of RECP technologies and processes, waste management and renewable energy solutions. A digital MRV system for emissions and traceability will close data and transparency gaps, enabling regulatory enforcement and compliance with international standards. This MRV system and its linkage with market compliance, will also incentivize supply chain actors to reduce their GHG emissions. Sector-specific emission baselines and carbon credit methodologies will be developed, positioning Pakistan to access emerging climate finance. Access to green finance will be facilitated through demonstration models and collective compliance solutions, reducing the cost burden for SMEs. By integrating technology, policy, and market interventions, the project directly supports Pakistan#s NDC target of 50% emissions reducti</narrative>
  </description>
